>>
Rule 1 (input tensor must have a numeric or boolean data type)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 2 (all dimensions of the input tensor must have non-negative sizes)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 3 (input tensor is either a scalar or has strictly positive shape dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 0 ∨ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 4 (non-empty real-valued input tensor has minimum element not exceeding maximum element)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8 then (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0) ∨ min(v_1) ≤ max(v_1)
